---
import StatusMark from '../../ui/StatusMark.vue';
import DesignSection from '../DesignSection.astro';
import DoDont from '../DoDont.astro';
import DontExamples from '../DontExamples.astro';
import SpecTable from '../SpecTable.astro';
import TokenTable from '../TokenTable.vue';

const RADII = [
  { name: '--radius-4', use: 'Popover tooltips, chart indicators.' },
  {
    name: '--radius-8',
    use: "Buttons, inputs, nav items, copy fields (Basecoat's rounded-md, --radius minus 2px).",
  },
  {
    name: '--radius-10',
    use: "Containers: table boxes, row lists, banners, notes, fields, empty states. Basecoat's dialog panel is 14px.",
  },
  {
    name: '--radius-full',
    use: 'Badges (tags) and round icon buttons. Not status pills: status uses the status mark.',
  },
];

const BORDERS = [
  { name: '--color-af-border', use: '1px. Container outlines, row rules.' },
  { name: '--color-af-border-strong', use: '1px. Anything a person can type in or press.' },
];

const SHADOWS = [
  {
    name: '--shadow-af-1',
    use: "Raised: the chart tooltip (through Basecoat's --shadow-xl), the open navigation drawer.",
  },
  { name: '--shadow-af-2', use: 'Overlay: dialogs.' },
  { name: '--color-af-scrim', use: 'The scrim behind a dialog.' },
];
---

<DesignSection id="border">
  <Fragment slot="definition"> Borders separate; they do not decorate. Corners are soft enough that a container feels like a surface holding its content, and consistent enough that nobody notices them. </Fragment>
  <TokenTable client:load tokens={RADII} specimen="radius" caption="Corner radius tokens, current values and uses" />
  <TokenTable client:load tokens={BORDERS} specimen="colour" caption="Border colour tokens and their current values" />
  <div class="design-prose">
    <ul>
      <li>Table headers are unfilled. No coloured stripe down one side of a container.</li>
      <li>
        The empty state (Basecoat's <code>empty</code>) is the only dashed border, and its content is centred, as Basecoat lays it out.
      </li>
      <li>
        Focus: Basecoat's controls draw a border and 3px halo from <code>--ring</code>; the portal's own links, nav items and summaries draw a 2px outline in the text colour, offset 2px. No element shows both.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <DoDont>
    <div slot="do" class="table-container af-box">
      <table class="table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Account</th><th>Status</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>CERN SSO</td><td><StatusMark tone="ok" label="Linked" /></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="do-note">let the container recede: unfilled header, pale rules, the data is the darkest thing in the box.</Fragment>
    <DontExamples slot="dont" kind="heavy-frame" />
    <Fragment slot="dont-note">use heavy outlines, filled headers or a coloured stripe down one side. The frame becomes louder than the content.</Fragment>
  </DoDont>
</DesignSection>

<DesignSection id="elevation">
  <Fragment slot="definition"> Elevation says what is temporarily on top. Everything that belongs to the page is flat. Only things that appear over the page have a shadow. </Fragment>
  <SpecTable columns={['Level', 'Token', 'Allowed on']} caption="Elevation levels">
    <tr>
      <td>Flat</td>
      <td>none</td>
      <td>Tables, sections, rows, banners, notes, sidebar, top bar, popover tooltips. Separated by a 1px border, never a shadow.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Raised</td>
      <td><code>--shadow-af-1</code></td>
      <td>The chart tooltip (through Basecoat's <code>--shadow-xl</code>), the open navigation drawer. No scrim.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Overlay</td>
      <td><code>--shadow-af-2</code> + <code>--color-af-scrim</code></td>
      <td>Dialogs. Scrim behind, focus trapped.</td>
    </tr>
  </SpecTable>
  <TokenTable client:load tokens={SHADOWS} caption="Shadow and scrim tokens and their current values" />
  <div class="design-cols">
    <div class="design-stage design-stage--subtle">
      <h3 class="design-label">Level 1: raised</h3>
      <div class="design-level design-level--raised">A raised surface</div>
    </div>
    <div class="design-stage design-stage--subtle">
      <h3 class="design-label">Level 2: overlay</h3>
      <div class="design-level design-level--overlay">An overlay surface</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="af-help">
    The two swatches show the shadow tokens; the real thing is the dialog (see Dialog and tooltip) and the chart tooltip (hover a bar in Chart). No background blur anywhere. In dark mode a shadow is hard to see, so both also carry a 1px light outline. Basecoat's own small shadows (<code>--shadow-xs</code>, <code>--shadow-sm</code>) resolve to none and its backdrop blur to 0.
  </p>
</DesignSection>
